cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these kernels, cite ANNY, whose body model they differentiate.
title: ANNY forward and backward kernels (Lean-emitted)
abstract: >-
  lean/Anny/SlangCodegen/*.lean restate the data-parallel stages of NAVER's
  ANNY body model as LeanSlang compute kernels on the drape kernels' layout
  (a params block at binding 0, flat float buffers): the blendshape sum and
  the linear-blend skinning of Sinew.SlangCodegen.Pheno.blendshape and
  Sinew.SlangCodegen.Lbs (lean/Sinew, V-Sekai-fire/sinew 36c926e), the
  sparse joint regressor of Sinew.SlangCodegen.Pheno.rbf as a CSR gemv over
  3-vectors, forward kinematics from 6D joint rotations (AGENTS.md rule 11),
  and the vertex residual of AnnyInverter's per-vertex loss, each with its
  vector-Jacobian product, so the in-guest L-BFGS-B (lean/Drape) can fit
  blendshape coefficients, joint rotations and the root translation to a
  target mesh. lake exe emit_anny writes them as Slang into slang/, and
  gen.sh compiles them to cpp/ (the in-guest CPU path) and SPIR-V (the GPU
  path). No ANNY source is copied. Local adaptations: the bind rotations
  (Sinew's skeleton_fit) are a stop-gradient; the phenotype-to-coefficient
  interpolation is not a kernel; long sums in the backward (dbone, dcoeffs)
  accumulate in df32 in vertex order; the regressor's backward runs the
  forward gemv on its transpose. Verified against a double-precision
  restatement and its central differences by tests/anny_kernels
  (gates/anny/kernels).
type: software
authors:
  - name: NAVER LABS Europe
repository-code: https://github.com/naver/anny
license: Apache-2.0
